1
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,660
Executive Producers: Ryuzo Shirakawa,
Akira Sato, Mitsuhisa Ishikawa

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:11,240
Planning and Original Concept:
Production I. G

3
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:16,750
Planning in Cooperation
with Mamoru Oshii (Team Oshii)

4
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:23,180
Character Designer: Katsuya Terada

5
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:30,730
Screenplay: Kenji Kamiyama

6
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,200
Technical Director: Shinji Takagi

7
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:41,860
Please take all your
belongings with you.

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,680
This will be the last train
going to Asakusa.

9
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:50,980
Animation Director: Kazuchika Kise

10
00:00:58,730 --> 00:01:02,020
Art Director: Yusuke Takeda

11
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:15,000
Director of Visual Concept:
Hisashi Ezura

12
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:33,320
Color Designer: Katsue Inoue

13
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:45,270
3D CGI: Tokumitsu Kifune

14
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:55,240
Filming: Miki Sakuma

15
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:54,300
Post Production Supervisor:
Keiichi Momose

16
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:04,350
Music: Yoshihiro Ike

17
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:18,600
We will be stopping at Asakusa shortly.
This will be the final stop.

18
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,400
Director: Hiroyuki Kitakubo

19
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,000
Saya!

20
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:05,250
Where is the chiropterate?

21
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:06,440
Inside.

22
00:04:08,490 --> 00:04:09,670
This sword's getting dull.

23
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:13,390
It's not sliding out of the sheath
as smoothly as it should.

24
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,700
- Get me a new one.
- That's not possible.

25
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:21,070
We don't have time because we just
identified another one of them.

26
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:23,990
Swords of that quality
are not easy to get.

27
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:41,420
What the...?

28
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,880
This isn't a chiropterate,
did we get the wrong guy?

29
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,320
It just hasn't changed form
yet, Louis. Now, shut up.

30
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:54,410
Wait a minute. Isn't this supposed
to be within your jurisdiction?

31
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,020
That's a regular
human corpse in there.

32
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:00,040
I've already checked
the military personnel

33
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,070
as well as
the civilian employees involved.

34
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:06,940
- What do you mean?
- Hey! David!

35
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:08,820
(David) They've
infiltrated the public.

36
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:11,090
You want me to investigate this?

37
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:13,230
Dave! Take a look inside!

38
00:05:14,330 --> 00:05:15,430
- Hey!
- Save it!

39
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,520
Oh, Jesus...

40
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,750
Wait! Saya!
Get ahold of yourself, now!

41
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:25,820
Not the same thing again.

42
00:05:26,690 --> 00:05:29,260
Do you want to announce it
to the whole world?

43
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,580
I can't do anything about it.

44
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:33,800
You know the way it is by now.

45
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:37,690
The orders from the top are
to hunt them down, no matter what.

46
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,780
- I really don't know anything.

47
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:49,660
It's all in there
and it's arranged accordingly.

48
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:51,470
You can go tomorrow.

49
00:05:52,110 --> 00:05:55,170
I'll have your school uniform
and ID ready by then.

50
00:05:56,010 --> 00:05:57,830
You better read through
the file carefully.

51
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,290
We know there's more than one...
Hey!

52
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,980
Hey, Saya!

53
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,270
Shit.

54
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,170
What the hell was that all about?

55
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,580
You asshole!

56
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:20,830
What did I do?!

57
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:23,110
Don't ever piss her off again!

58
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:24,720
- But...
- Listen!

59
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,800
As far as we know,
she's the only remaining original.

60
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:31,710
Original?

61
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:20,530
So the tap was still running
when you found her.

62
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:24,970
Calm down.
You don't have to cry.

63
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:33,220
I'm not too sure, but I heard Mari
was going out with an American soldier.

64
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:40,890
Mari from Charade's
committed suicide.

65
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:44,620
Stupid girl.
She didn't have to kill herself.

66
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:48,000
Maybe she's got the "clap."

67
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,390
You can't get upset over
a minor thing

68
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:53,700
if you're doing business
with American soldiers.

69
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:58,210
Did you hear about the suicide
at the base school last month?

70
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:01,710
There seem to be
a lot of them lately.

71
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:05,220
Apparently, everybody's really
uptight about it.

72
00:08:05,850 --> 00:08:09,220
How terrible.
I hope this doesn't affect business.

73
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:13,880
It can't be helped if we're going
to make a living off the base.

74
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:15,420
Huh?

75
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:21,170
It can't be helped if we're going
to make a living off the base.

76
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:10,880
Aren't you Japanese?
You are not a student here, are you?

77
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:14,380
Did you pass through the office?

78
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:19,780
Hey, hold on a second!

79
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:24,220
Where is the principal's office?

80
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:25,220
Huh?

81
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:30,060
Come in.

82
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,810
Sir, this young lady here...

83
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:35,500
Ahh, Saya. You're late.

84
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:37,580
I want you to say hello
to the principal.

85
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,130
Hello. You do speak English?

86
00:10:44,450 --> 00:10:45,270
(David) Of course.

87
00:10:45,890 --> 00:10:49,190
Well then, you can go see
some classes this afternoon.

88
00:10:49,990 --> 00:10:54,110
But with the Halloween party coming
up we may not get much work done.

89
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,740
Thank you very much for your help.
Goodbye.

90
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:08,850
Who was that girl?

91
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,600
She came on an introduction.

92
00:11:10,990 --> 00:11:13,180
She wants to join classes
for a few days.

93
00:11:15,110 --> 00:11:16,860
- Um, excuse me, sir...
- Huh?

94
00:11:17,290 --> 00:11:20,260
About the party tomorrow?

95
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,850
Not that again.

96
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:24,780
I thought we were over that by now.

97
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,710
Yes, sir, but it isn't long
since the terrible incident.

98
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:32,550
Have the students recovered
from the death of their friend?

99
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:36,740
That's why we're having this party.
I've had enough of this.

100
00:11:37,650 --> 00:11:39,150
Now, get back to work.

101
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:52,000
What the hell is this outfit?

102
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,680
I'm not sure. It's supposed to be
a Japanese high school uniform.

103
00:11:56,480 --> 00:12:00,070
At any rate, another fake corpse
was found here last night,

104
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:01,420
and it's the same pattern.

105
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,000
It's happening awfully fast.

106
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,660
I told you
there was more than one of them.

107
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:11,180
We'll never find them
once they go into hibernation.

108
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:13,280
We have to find them
before we get another corpse.

109
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:15,930
You just listen for them.

110
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:17,970
And get the sword.

111
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,340
(David) I know.

112
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:51,960
All right, that's it for today.

113
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:54,400
Tomorrow we'll have
morning classes only.

114
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:57,170
- I'm not through yet.

115
00:12:57,560 --> 00:13:00,240
Those getting things ready for
the dance meet in the assembly room,

116
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,360
the rest of you can stay here
and get ready...

117
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,840
Hey, are you Japanese?

118
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,620
(Teacher) ..or old Pumpkinhead
will get you.

119
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:14,670
Leave me alone.

120
00:13:16,450 --> 00:13:17,210
Weirdo!

121
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:19,960
Come on, Linda, let's go.

122
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:12,830
So, this is their "dining room" then.

123
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,090
Oh, you scared me.

124
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,960
What were you doing here?

125
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:38,270
Nothing. I thought I had a headache.

126
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,340
But it's gone now.

127
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:42,100
Oh. Wait!

128
00:15:44,910 --> 00:15:46,900
Hold on a minute!

129
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:12,370
Come on, the band's
going to start any minute now.

130
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,610
- Sir?
- What is it, Sharon?

131
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,540
Aren't you going to put on
your costumes? What's the matter?

132
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:27,390
Linda told me she's not feeling very
well. It might be her anaemia again.

133
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:30,610
I thought I'd go with her
to the infirmary.

134
00:17:33,830 --> 00:17:36,560
Again? Well, OK.
You don't need me, do you?

135
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:40,470
- No, sir.
- Join us when she feels better.

136
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:42,460
- You girls be careful, now.
- OK.

137
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,470
Are you OK?

138
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,030
It won't be too long.

139
00:18:16,270 --> 00:18:18,370
I'd like
to take it easy once in a while.

140
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:20,510
Especially on a day like this.

141
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:28,520
This isn't a very fun way
to spend Halloween, is it?

142
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:37,220
Don't worry,
it's only minor anaemia.

143
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,060
She should feel better any minute.

144
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:44,020
You should really try
not to worry too much,

145
00:18:44,750 --> 00:18:46,470
and just enjoy the festivity.

146
00:18:47,930 --> 00:18:49,810
What are you girls
gonna dress up as?

147
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:53,580
Witches? Vampires, maybe?

148
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:01,290
A-ha, here it is.

149
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:04,830
Mm? Sharon, what is it?
What's happening?

150
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,870
You...

151
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,380
Hey!

152
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:46,050
Hey!

153
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:49,920
Listen to me!

154
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:52,910
Listen, just forget what you just saw.

155
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:10,440
Why... What is this...
You are...

156
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:17,150
Linda wasn't feeling well.
She was just sleeping...

157
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:18,610
Linda...

158
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,550
Linda...

159
00:20:41,610 --> 00:20:44,580
What? What is this?

160
00:20:45,610 --> 00:20:46,600
Linda...

161
00:21:30,290 --> 00:21:32,810
Hey, Mama-san, where's my beer?

162
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:37,650
Oh, I'm sorry.

163
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:42,260
Excuse me. I'll be right back.

164
00:22:38,050 --> 00:22:40,960
I don't believe it!
There's actually three of them.

165
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:43,050
Turn left here.

166
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:44,930
Aren't they at the base?

167
00:22:45,690 --> 00:22:47,640
- There's the other one.
- Oh, what?

168
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:50,180
It's all over if we lose this one.
Hurry!

169
00:24:24,320 --> 00:24:25,830
Ted, have you seen Sharon?

170
00:24:26,470 --> 00:24:27,430
No, I haven't.

171
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:41,050
It's a fake!

172
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:11,430
What are you doing?

173
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:12,900
Run for it!

174
00:26:29,580 --> 00:26:31,080
This one is also
heading for the base.

175
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:34,860
Have the military stand down!
And Louis, look for Saya!

176
00:27:06,060 --> 00:27:09,550
(Laughs) Excuse me, ma'am.
Are you trying to surprise me now?

177
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:13,000
You're a teacher, ma'am,
what are you doing here?

178
00:27:13,540 --> 00:27:15,620
Shouldn't you be at the party?

179
00:27:16,190 --> 00:27:18,390
Help! A student
changed into a monster!

180
00:27:19,470 --> 00:27:23,470
You're not pulling that one on me,
even if it is Halloween tonight.

181
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:26,860
No, really!
It just attacked me over there!

182
00:27:27,340 --> 00:27:31,720
Kids these days, they really do
get into these tricks of theirs.

183
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:34,910
It's not a trick!
Please, believe me! Help me!

184
00:27:38,980 --> 00:27:41,080
Hey, just try to calm down
a little, ma'am.

185
00:27:45,170 --> 00:27:48,470
We used to play little tricks
on teachers we didn't like.

186
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:51,820
But kids have no reason
to hate a pretty one like yourself.

187
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:55,320
It's more likely a kid
wanted some attention...

188
00:27:56,780 --> 00:27:58,520
Whoa!

189
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:38,380
Run!

190
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:51,740
Hey! Halt! Where are you going?
This area's off-limits!

191
00:28:56,730 --> 00:28:57,730
- Please...
- Stop!

192
00:28:58,200 --> 00:29:00,390
- Help us!
- Who are you, ma'am?

193
00:29:01,370 --> 00:29:02,570
And who is this kid with you?

194
00:29:03,730 --> 00:29:04,450
She's...

195
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:08,380
Hey, what happened to you?
You're bleeding.

196
00:29:10,450 --> 00:29:11,660
(Nurse) We've just been attacked!

197
00:29:12,660 --> 00:29:15,120
Wait here. I'll call headquarters.

198
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:17,440
Huh? (Coughs)

199
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:31,070
Go inside.

200
00:29:37,910 --> 00:29:39,340
What did you just do?

201
00:29:40,650 --> 00:29:43,340
What are you trying to do here?

202
00:29:43,850 --> 00:29:45,180
Shut up!

203
00:29:55,830 --> 00:29:58,920
Listen! Anyone who is
marked by "them" or

204
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:01,860
anyone who has seen "their" real form,
isn't allowed to live.

205
00:30:03,100 --> 00:30:05,800
So, we've got to kill "them"
before "they" get us.

206
00:30:07,940 --> 00:30:09,410
What are "they"?

207
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:14,880
Demons. They live off human blood.

208
00:30:33,300 --> 00:30:36,500
Shit! Isn't there something?

209
00:30:39,600 --> 00:30:40,700
Like what?

210
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:42,000
A weapon.

211
00:30:46,780 --> 00:30:47,640
Here...

212
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:50,240
That won't kill them.

213
00:30:50,850 --> 00:30:52,210
They won't die

214
00:30:52,210 --> 00:30:55,180
unless they lose enough blood
in one blow.

215
00:30:56,220 --> 00:30:58,280
Then what is this gun for?

216
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:00,650
You may need it.

217
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:05,890
You can kill yourself as a last resort.

218
00:31:09,790 --> 00:31:13,360
Dear God help me!
Don't!

219
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:20,650
Why me?

220
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:23,810
Who are you?

221
00:31:26,450 --> 00:31:30,750
Why did you help me?

222
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:36,990
You're lucky. I can't kill "humans."

223
00:32:03,060 --> 00:32:04,080
Shut up!

224
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:20,860
Wait! Don't shoot!

225
00:32:54,120 --> 00:32:55,220
David!

226
00:32:55,580 --> 00:32:56,340
Saya...

227
00:32:58,610 --> 00:32:59,910
Saya, is that you?!

228
00:33:03,780 --> 00:33:04,970
Open the door!

229
00:33:37,800 --> 00:33:39,160
Fuck! Oh...

230
00:33:49,030 --> 00:33:49,880
Saya!

231
00:33:58,670 --> 00:34:00,260
I can't take this anymore.

232
00:34:04,340 --> 00:34:05,570
Don't give up!

233
00:34:05,910 --> 00:34:07,000
Get the car!

234
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,640
Run the doors down!

235
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:36,240
Shit!

236
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:47,610
Saya!

237
00:34:52,450 --> 00:34:53,270
Sword!

238
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:05,560
(David) You all right?

239
00:35:05,560 --> 00:35:06,610
Saya!

240
00:35:28,620 --> 00:35:29,370
(Saya) Don't!

241
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,670
It's preparing to fly. Take the car.

242
00:35:46,270 --> 00:35:47,490
It's going to take off.

243
00:35:54,860 --> 00:35:55,990
Hurry!

244
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:01,480
Louis here.

245
00:36:02,220 --> 00:36:03,890
(David) 'The target
is heading for the runway.

246
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:09,230
'We need to get to the woman
who saw the demon before the cops.'

247
00:36:10,170 --> 00:36:11,040
Roger, you got it.

248
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:27,170
Shit, it's gonna jump onto it!

249
00:36:27,170 --> 00:36:28,670
Damn it to hell!

250
00:36:29,070 --> 00:36:29,880
(Saya) Just leave it.

251
00:36:58,420 --> 00:37:00,700
- Get closer!
- Don't make it sound so easy!

252
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,070
Saya, where are you going?
You cannot leave!

253
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:17,350
Saya!

254
00:39:53,030 --> 00:39:54,550
And this is all I know.

255
00:39:55,690 --> 00:39:58,860
I've told you everything
I've seen with my own eyes.

256
00:40:00,550 --> 00:40:02,610
Even though
I'm not sure you believe me.

257
00:40:04,580 --> 00:40:07,800
No, no. We just want to hear
what happened, madam.

258
00:40:09,450 --> 00:40:11,210
I'm not even sure
what really happened.

259
00:40:12,780 --> 00:40:16,560
When I returned to the infirmary,
what should have been Linda's...

260
00:40:17,350 --> 00:40:20,270
I mean, the strange creature's
remains were gone.

261
00:40:21,380 --> 00:40:22,720
No sign of a struggle.

262
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:25,640
Everything had been wiped clean.

263
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:28,520
The principal, the teachers,

264
00:40:29,390 --> 00:40:32,810
nobody would believe me
when I told them what had happened.

265
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:40,240
I know, the man that was with her,
she called him David.

266
00:40:40,940 --> 00:40:42,860
Doesn't he work in this building?

267
00:40:43,640 --> 00:40:46,570
He would know what happened.
Where is he?

268
00:40:50,470 --> 00:40:53,080
Madam,
no one fitting your description

269
00:40:53,680 --> 00:40:55,370
works or is stationed at this base.

270
00:40:55,820 --> 00:40:58,550
- That can't be, he...
- I'm sorry, madam,

271
00:40:58,920 --> 00:41:00,760
we don't have
any further information.

272
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:13,090
Before you go, the girl you saw...
did she look like this?

273
00:42:49,170 --> 00:42:54,570
After all,
I never understood what I saw.

274
00:42:55,670 --> 00:43:01,170
That girl Saya and the creatures
she killed all remained a mystery.

275
00:43:01,780 --> 00:43:05,480
Only two students were noted
as having left for other schools.

276
00:43:07,250 --> 00:43:11,210
Could she still be somewhere
around the base?

277
00:43:12,460 --> 00:43:15,760
Is she still fighting those creatures?

278
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:20,490
Just as we humans continue
to kill each other.

279
00:43:22,170 --> 00:43:25,830
That beautiful,
yet dangerous living thing

280
00:43:29,710 --> 00:43:32,510
(Radio) 'The liberation front has
attacked the American Blake base.

281
00:43:33,070 --> 00:43:36,200
'In retaliation,
B-52s from Yokota base in Japan

282
00:43:36,460 --> 00:43:39,370
'have been ordered
to fly to North Vietnam.'

283
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:09,080
Readjusted By Sooraj
